[Term]
id: PATO:0001018
name: obsolete physical quality
alt_id: PATO:0002079
def: "OBSOLETE. A quality of a physical entity that exists through action of continuants at the physical level of organisation in relation to other entities." [PATOC:GVG]
comment: Obsoleted in https://github.com/pato-ontology/pato/issues/602. The 'physical level of organisation in relation to other entities' criterion has never been operationalised, and existing classification was haphazard (time, flavor, odor, movement quality, neuron projection quality all sat under physical quality despite not being 'physical level' in any defensible sense). Children have been moved up to physical object characteristic; outliers (time, movement quality, neuron projection quality) require a follow-up sweep to find more appropriate parents.
synonym: "physical quality" EXACT [OBO:legacy]
synonym: "relational physical quality" EXACT []
xref: Wikipedia:Physical_property
is_obsolete: true
replaced_by: PATO:0001241

