[Term]
id: PATO:0040060
name: absence of anatomical entity
def: "A quality denoting the lack of an anatomical entity or cellular component." [thefreedictionary.:thefreedictionary.]
comment: Absence of anatomical entity should only be used when all of the entity is absent. For example, absent teeth would mean all teeth are absent not some teeth are absent.
subset: absent_slim
synonym: "anatomical entity absence" EXACT []
is_a: PATO:0000051 ! morphology
is_a: PATO:0040058 ! absence of physical object
created_by: http://orcid.org/0000-0001-5208-3432

[Term]
id: PATO:0040070
