[Term]
id: PATO:0102001
name: modifier characteristic
def: "A characteristic used to describe another characteristic." [https://github.com/pato-ontology/pato/issues/602]
comment: Instances of modifier characteristic should NOT be linked to their bearers via 'characteristic of' (RO:0000052) or its inverse 'has characteristic' (RO:0000053). Use 'has modifier' (RO:0002573) to connect a modifier characteristic to the characteristic it modifies. This keeps 'characteristic of' / 'has characteristic' restricted to entity-or-process-to-characteristic relations.
synonym: "meta characteristic" RELATED [OBO:earlier-draft]
is_a: PATO:0000001 ! characteristic
created_by: https://orcid.org/0000-0002-7356-1779
creation_date: 2026-05-05T00:00:00Z

[Term]
id: PATO:0102002
name: comparative modifier characteristic
def: "A modifier characteristic determined by comparison to a reference." [https://github.com/pato-ontology/pato/issues/602]
comment: A comparative modifier characteristic is relational - its identity (e.g. increased vs decreased, abnormal vs normal) is fixed by comparison to a reference. The broader 'modifier characteristic' also covers non-comparative modifiers (intensity, magnitude, secondary).
synonym: "comparison modifier" RELATED [OBO:earlier-draft]
synonym: "state modifier" RELATED [OBO:earlier-draft]
is_a: PATO:0102001 ! modifier characteristic
created_by: https://orcid.org/0000-0002-7356-1779
creation_date: 2026-05-05T00:00:00Z

[Term]
id: PATO:0102003
name: increased
def: "A comparative modifier characteristic indicating that the bearer characteristic has a value greater than a reference." [https://github.com/pato-ontology/pato/issues/602]
comment: Usage (agreed uPheno call 2026-06-12): 'increased' is only to be used to define pre-coordinated value terms via 'has modifier' (RO:0002573), e.g. 'increased weight' EquivalentTo 'weight and has_modifier some increased'. Do NOT use 'increased' directly in phenotype patterns, and do NOT use it as an is_a parent of a domain characteristic. If a pre-coordinated value term exists for the bearer and direction, use that term; if none exists, request that it be added. Distinct from the now-obsolete PATO:0002300 (increased quality), which was a grouping class for pre-coordinated physical/process qualities.
is_a: PATO:0102002 ! comparative modifier characteristic
relationship: is_opposite_of PATO:0102004 ! decreased
created_by: https://orcid.org/0000-0002-7356-1779
creation_date: 2026-05-05T00:00:00Z

[Term]
id: PATO:0102004
name: decreased
def: "A comparative modifier characteristic indicating that the bearer characteristic has a value less than a reference." [https://github.com/pato-ontology/pato/issues/602]
comment: Usage (agreed uPheno call 2026-06-12): 'decreased' is only to be used to define pre-coordinated value terms via 'has modifier' (RO:0002573), e.g. 'decreased weight' EquivalentTo 'weight and has_modifier some decreased'. Do NOT use 'decreased' directly in phenotype patterns, and do NOT use it as an is_a parent of a domain characteristic. If a pre-coordinated value term exists for the bearer and direction, use that term; if none exists, request that it be added. Distinct from the now-obsolete PATO:0002301 (decreased quality), which was a grouping class for pre-coordinated physical/process qualities.
is_a: PATO:0102002 ! comparative modifier characteristic
relationship: is_opposite_of PATO:0102003 ! increased
created_by: https://orcid.org/0000-0002-7356-1779
creation_date: 2026-05-05T00:00:00Z

[Term]
id: PATO:0103000
name: obsolete quantitative
def: "OBSOLETE. A quality of an entity that can be represented numerically, including anything that can be counted, measured, or given a numerical value." [https://libguides.macalester.edu/c.php?g=527786&p=3608639, https://www.nnlm.gov/guides/data-glossary/quantitative-data]
comment: Obsoleted in https://github.com/pato-ontology/pato/issues/602. The qualitative/quantitative dichotomy has no role in the new upper model. The single direct child (amount, PATO:0000070) has been moved under physical object characteristic.
is_obsolete: true
created_by: https://orcid.org/0000-0001-8314-2140

[Term]
id: PATO:0103001
name: total mass
def: "A quantitative quality that represents the sum of all 'mass' qualities of the component parts that constitute a whole entity. The total mass quality inheres in the whole entity and reflects the aggregate measure of mass across all its components, such that changes in the mass of individual components may not necessarily correspond to equivalent changes in the total mass of the whole.\n\nExample of usage: \"total body mass\" represents the sum of the masses of all tissues and organs in the body, while \"liver mass\" represents only the mass of the liver. An increase in liver mass does not necessarily mean an increase in total body mass, as the mass of other organs or tissues may decrease simultaneously." []
is_a: PATO:0000125 ! mass
property_value: dc:date "2025-04-10T16:14:12Z" xsd:dateTime
property_value: terms3:contributor https://orcid.org/0000-0001-8314-2140

[Term]
id: PATO:0103002
name: increased total mass
def: "A total mass which is higher than normal or average." []
is_a: PATO:0001563 ! increased mass
is_a: PATO:0103001 ! total mass
intersection_of: PATO:0103001 ! total mass
intersection_of: RO:0015007 PATO:0000461 ! increased in magnitude relative to normal
property_value: dc:date "2025-04-10T16:25:35Z" xsd:dateTime
property_value: terms3:contributor https://orcid.org/0000-0001-8314-2140

[Term]
id: PATO:0103003
name: decreased total mass
def: "A total mass which is lower than normal or average." []
