[Term]
id: PATO:0103304
name: segmental allotetraploid
def: "An allotetraploid quality inhering in a bearer by virtue of the bearer's two parental subgenomes being only partially differentiated (partially homeologous)." [PMID:29985538, PMID:33005183]
comment: The two parental subgenomes are partially homeologous, producing inconsistent chromosome pairing. Cultivated peanut (Arachis hypogaea) is an example.
subset: cell_quality
subset: value_slim
is_a: PATO:0103302 ! allotetraploid
property_value: terms:contributor https://orcid.org/0000-0001-9076-6066
creation_date: 2026-06-17T22:04:36Z

