[Term]
id: PATO:0104351
name: filiform
def: "A shape quality inhering in a bearer by virtue of the bearer being long, very slender, and circular or nearly circular in transverse section, thereby resembling a thread." [https://www.mobot.org/mobot/latindict/keyDetail.aspx?keyWord=filiform, https://www.upov.int/documents/d/upov/tgp-documents-en-tgp_14.pdf]
comment: Requested for FLOPO; corresponding temporary class: FLOPO_0985001.
