creation_date: 2026-09-18T00:00:00Z

[Term]
id: PATO:0104352
name: hastate
def: "A shape quality inhering in a bearer by virtue of the bearer being flat and having two approximately triangular basal lobes directed outward to either side of the main axis." [https://plantnet.rbgsyd.nsw.gov.au/cgi-bin/NSWfl.pl?glossary=yes&ill=Fig.+7+I&page=nswfl&term=hastate, https://www.mobot.org/mobot/latindict/keyDetail.aspx?keyWord=hastatus, https://www.upov.int/documents/d/upov/tgp-documents-en-tgp_14.pdf]
comment: Requested for FLOPO; corresponding temporary class: FLOPO_0985002. Distinguished from arrow-shaped (PATO:0001881; synonym sagittate), whose basal lobes point backward rather than outward.
subset: value_slim
is_a: PATO:0000052 ! shape
property_value: terms:contributor https://orcid.org/0000-0001-8149-5890
creation_date: 2026-09-18T00:00:00Z

[Term]
id: PATO:0104353
name: reflexed
def: "A shape quality inhering in a bearer by virtue of the bearer being abruptly bent backward or abaxially downward." [https://sweetgum.nybg.org/science/glossary/glossary-details/?irn=1363, https://www.upov.int/documents/d/upov/tgp-documents-en-tgp_14.pdf]
comment: Requested for FLOPO; corresponding temporary class: FLOPO_0985003. Distinguished from the curvature qualities recurved (PATO:0002211) and retrorse (PATO:0002237): a reflexed bearer is bent at an angle rather than curved.
subset: value_slim
is_a: PATO:0000617 ! bent
property_value: terms:contributor https://orcid.org/0000-0001-8149-5890
creation_date: 2026-09-18T00:00:00Z

[Term]
id: PATO:0104354
name: winged
def: "A shape quality inhering in a bearer by virtue of the bearer having one or more conspicuous, thin, flattened extensions that project from its main body." [https://sweetgum.nybg.org/science/glossary/glossary-details/?irn=2950, https://www.aos.org/orchids/orchid-basics/orchid-glossary]
comment: Requested for FLOPO; corresponding temporary class: FLOPO_0985004.
subset: value_slim
synonym: "alate" EXACT []
is_a: PATO:0000052 ! shape
property_value: terms:contributor https://orcid.org/0000-0001-8149-5890
creation_date: 2026-09-18T00:00:00Z

[Term]
id: PATO:0104355
name: ascending
def: "An oblique orientation quality inhering in a bearer by virtue of the bearer being directed gradually upward at an oblique angle." [https://www.upov.int/documents/d/upov/tgp-documents-en-tgp_14.pdf]
comment: Requested for FLOPO; corresponding temporary class: FLOPO_0985005. Some sources restrict ascending to a bearer with an initially horizontal or spreading base; that restriction is not part of this definition.
subset: value_slim
is_a: PATO:0002481 ! oblique orientation
property_value: terms:contributor https://orcid.org/0000-0001-8149-5890
creation_date: 2026-09-18T00:00:00Z

[Term]
id: PATO:0104356
name: spreading
def: "An orientation quality inhering in a bearer by virtue of the bearer being directed outward and diverging from a principal axis." [https://www.upov.int/documents/d/upov/tgp-documents-en-tgp_14.pdf]
comment: Requested for FLOPO; corresponding temporary class: FLOPO_0985006. Distinguished from radiating (PATO:0005005), which requires expansion from a centre point, and from divergent from (PATO:0002424), which inheres in a bearer whose parts extend in different directions. Not a relational quality: like ascending and the other orientation qualities, spreading describes the direction of the bearer itself within its frame of reference (the axis from which it arises), and does not relate the bearer to a second, independent entity.
subset: value_slim
is_a: PATO:0000133 ! orientation
property_value: terms:contributor https://orcid.org/0000-0001-8149-5890
creation_date: 2026-09-18T00:00:00Z

[Term]
id: PATO:0104357
name: lanate
def: "A pilosity quality inhering in a bearer by virtue of the bearer being covered with long, somewhat matted and tangled trichomes that give a wool-like appearance." [https://sweetgum.nybg.org/science/glossary/glossary-details/?irn=939, https://www.upov.int/documents/d/upov/tgp-documents-en-tgp_14.pdf]
comment: Requested for FLOPO; corresponding temporary class: FLOPO_0985007. Distinguished from tomentose (PATO:0002341), whose hairs are shorter, denser and more closely matted.
subset: value_slim
synonym: "woolly" RELATED []
is_a: PATO:0000454 ! hairy
property_value: terms:contributor https://orcid.org/0000-0001-8149-5890
creation_date: 2026-09-18T00:00:00Z

[Term]
id: PATO:0104358
name: sericeous
def: "A pilosity quality inhering in a bearer by virtue of the bearer being covered with long, soft, slender, appressed trichomes that give a silk-like appearance." [https://sweetgum.nybg.org/science/glossary/glossary-details/?irn=1450, https://www.upov.int/documents/d/upov/tgp-documents-en-tgp_14.pdf]
comment: Requested for FLOPO; corresponding temporary class: FLOPO_0985008.
subset: value_slim
synonym: "silky" RELATED []
is_a: PATO:0000454 ! hairy
property_value: terms:contributor https://orcid.org/0000-0001-8149-5890
creation_date: 2026-09-18T00:00:00Z

[Term]
id: PATO:0104359
name: entire
def: "An edge shape quality inhering in a bearer by virtue of the bearer's edge being continuous and even, without teeth, lobes, or other incisions." [https://sweetgum.nybg.org/science/glossary/glossary-details/?irn=626, https://www.upov.int/documents/d/upov/tgp-documents-en-tgp_14.pdf]
comment: Requested for FLOPO; corresponding temporary class: FLOPO_0985009. Narrower than unserrated (PATO:0001975): an entire edge also lacks lobes and crenations.
subset: value_slim
synonym: "entire margin" RELATED []
is_a: PATO:0001975 ! unserrated
property_value: terms:contributor https://orcid.org/0000-0001-8149-5890
creation_date: 2026-09-18T00:00:00Z

[Term]
id: PATO:0104360
name: annual life span
def: "A life span quality inhering in a bearer by virtue of the bearer's expected natural life span being no more than one year." [https://sweetgum.nybg.org/science/glossary/glossary-details/?irn=272, https://www.rhs.org.uk/advice/beginners-guide/glossary]
comment: Requested for FLOPO; corresponding temporary class: FLOPO_0985010. Annual, biennial and perennial life span are absolute-duration qualities and together partition expected natural life span; the existing siblings increased, decreased and normal life span are relative-magnitude qualities. The synonym annual is RELATED because outside life-history descriptions the word denotes a yearly frequency.
subset: value_slim
synonym: "annual" RELATED []
is_a: PATO:0000050 ! life span
property_value: terms:contributor https://orcid.org/0000-0001-8149-5890
creation_date: 2026-09-18T00:00:00Z

[Term]
id: PATO:0104361
name: perennial life span
def: "A life span quality inhering in a bearer by virtue of the bearer's expected natural life span being more than two years." [https://sweetgum.nybg.org/science/glossary/glossary-details/?irn=1182, https://www.rhs.org.uk/advice/beginners-guide/glossary]
comment: Requested for FLOPO; corresponding temporary class: FLOPO_0985011. Absolute-duration quality; see annual life span (PATO:0104360) for the partition with biennial life span (PATO:0104367).
subset: value_slim
synonym: "perennial" EXACT []
is_a: PATO:0000050 ! life span
property_value: terms:contributor https://orcid.org/0000-0001-8149-5890
creation_date: 2026-09-18T00:00:00Z

[Term]
id: PATO:0104362
name: dissected
def: "A split quality inhering in a bearer by virtue of the bearer being divided, at least partially, by incisions into visibly distinct segments that may remain connected." [https://plantnet.rbgsyd.nsw.gov.au/cgi-bin/NSWfl.pl?glossary=yes&page=nswfl&alpha=D-E]
comment: Requested for FLOPO; corresponding temporary class: FLOPO_0985012. Distinguished from cut (PATO:0001978), which requires regular, deep incisions, and from lobed (PATO:0001979). No incision-depth threshold is implied.
subset: value_slim
is_a: PATO:0001786 ! split
property_value: terms:contributor https://orcid.org/0000-0001-8149-5890
creation_date: 2026-09-18T00:00:00Z

[Term]
id: PATO:0104363
name: clasping
def: "An attachment quality inhering in a bearer by virtue of the bearer at least partially enclosing an axis to which it is attached." [https://plantnet.rbgsyd.nsw.gov.au/cgi-bin/NSWfl.pl?glossary=yes&page=nswfl&alpha=C, https://sweetgum.nybg.org/science/glossary/glossary-details/?irn=467]
comment: Requested for FLOPO; corresponding temporary class: FLOPO_0985013. Amplexicaul (a leaf base clasping the stem) is a narrower botanical use. Relational quality: the definition refers to a second entity, the axis to which the bearer is attached, so the term lives under attachment quality with sessile (sensu botany) (PATO:0001436) rather than under position.
subset: relational_slim
subset: value_slim
synonym: "amplexicaul" NARROW []
is_a: PATO:0001435 ! attachment quality
property_value: terms:contributor https://orcid.org/0000-0001-8149-5890
creation_date: 2026-09-18T00:00:00Z

[Term]
id: PATO:0104364
name: mealy
def: "A texture quality inhering in a bearer by virtue of the bearer being covered with a coarse, flour-like powder." [https://ausflora.net/wp-content/uploads/2017/06/flora-of-australia-glossary-e28094-ferns-cycads-conifers-and-vascular-plants.pdf, https://plantnet.rbgsyd.nsw.gov.au/cgi-bin/NSWfl.pl?glossary=yes&page=nswfl&alpha=F-H, https://plantnet.rbgsyd.nsw.gov.au/cgi-bin/NSWfl.pl?glossary=yes&page=nswfl&alpha=M-O]
comment: Requested for FLOPO; corresponding temporary class: FLOPO_0985014. Some glossaries distinguish coarse mealy powder from fine farina (farinose); farinose is therefore not added as a synonym.
subset: value_slim
is_a: PATO:0000150 ! texture
property_value: terms:contributor https://orcid.org/0000-0001-8149-5890
creation_date: 2026-09-18T00:00:00Z

[Term]
id: PATO:0104365
name: plicate
def: "A folded quality inhering in a bearer by virtue of the bearer being folded back and forth longitudinally like a fan." [https://ausflora.net/wp-content/uploads/2017/06/flora-of-australia-glossary-e28094-ferns-cycads-conifers-and-vascular-plants.pdf, https://plantnet.rbgsyd.nsw.gov.au/cgi-bin/NSWfl.pl?glossary=yes&page=nswfl&alpha=P]
comment: Requested for FLOPO; corresponding temporary class: FLOPO_0985015. A single longitudinal fold does not satisfy the definition.
subset: value_slim
synonym: "pleated" RELATED []
is_a: PATO:0001910 ! folded
property_value: terms:contributor https://orcid.org/0000-0001-8149-5890
creation_date: 2026-09-18T00:00:00Z

[Term]
id: PATO:0104366
name: floccose
def: "A pilosity quality inhering in a bearer by virtue of the bearer having tufts of long, soft hairs that tend to rub off as small wool-like masses." [https://ausflora.net/wp-content/uploads/2017/06/flora-of-australia-glossary-e28094-ferns-cycads-conifers-and-vascular-plants.pdf, https://plantnet.rbgsyd.nsw.gov.au/cgi-bin/NSWfl.pl?glossary=yes&page=nswfl&alpha=F-H, https://www.upov.int/documents/d/upov/tgp-documents-en-tgp_14.pdf]
comment: Requested for FLOPO; corresponding temporary class: FLOPO_0985016. Cottony does not by itself imply that the hairs rub off, so it is a related synonym only.
subset: value_slim
synonym: "cottony" RELATED []
synonym: "flocculose" NARROW []
is_a: PATO:0000454 ! hairy
property_value: terms:contributor https://orcid.org/0000-0001-8149-5890
creation_date: 2026-09-18T00:00:00Z

[Term]
id: PATO:0104367
name: biennial life span
def: "A life span quality inhering in a bearer by virtue of the bearer's expected natural life span being more than one year and no more than two years." [https://ausflora.net/wp-content/uploads/2017/06/flora-of-australia-glossary-e28094-ferns-cycads-conifers-and-vascular-plants.pdf, https://www.rhs.org.uk/advice/beginners-guide/glossary]
comment: Requested for FLOPO; corresponding temporary class: FLOPO_0987000. Absolute-duration quality; see annual life span (PATO:0104360) for the partition with perennial life span (PATO:0104361). The synonym biennial is RELATED because outside life-history descriptions the word denotes a two-yearly frequency.
subset: value_slim
synonym: "biennial" RELATED []
is_a: PATO:0000050 ! life span
property_value: terms:contributor https://orcid.org/0000-0001-8149-5890
creation_date: 2026-10-01T00:00:00Z

[Term]
id: PCO:0000000
name: collection of organisms
def: "A material entity that consists of two or more organisms, viruses, or viroids." []
comment: May be of the same or different species.
is_a: BFO:0000027
is_a: PCO:0000031 ! organismal entity

[Term]
id: PCO:0000001
name: population of organisms
def: "A collection of organisms, all of the same species, that live in the same place." []
comment: It is sometimes difficult to define the physical boundaries of a population. In the case of sexually reproducing organisms, the individuals within a population have the potential to reproduce with one another during the course of their lifetimes. 'Community', as often used to describe a group of humans, is a type of population of organisms. \n\nClasses for population already  exist in IDO ('organism population', IDO_0000509) and OBI ('population', OBI_0000181). The definitions should be standardized across OBO Foundry ontologies and only one term used.
is_a: PCO:0000018 ! single-species collection of organisms

[Term]
id: PCO:0000002
name: ecological community
def: "A multi-species collection of organisms of at least two different species, living in a particular area. Must have at least two populations of different species as members." []
comment: Ecological community is defined broadly here, but includes both ecological interactions (inherited from parent term community) and spatial co-existence. It may be used to describe every organisms living in an area, but is often used to refer only to organisms of a particular taxon or guild (e.g., the plant community, the insect community, the herbivore community). The word community, as it often used to describe a group of humans living together, is a type of single-species collection of organisms, not an ecological community.
is_a: PCO:0000029 ! multi-species collection of organisms

[Term]
id: PCO:0000003
name: quality of a population
def: "A quality that inheres in a population of organisms." []
comment: Includes qualities like population size, population growth rate, carrying capacity, immigration rate, emigration rate, fecundity, and death rate. A population quality may depend on the qualities of individual organisms in the population, but cannot be measured or described for a single organism. This term may be replaced by a PATO term.
is_a: PATO:0002003 ! population quality
intersection_of: PATO:0002003 ! population quality
intersection_of: RO:0000052 PCO:0000001 ! characteristic of population of organisms
relationship: RO:0000052 PCO:0000001 ! characteristic of population of organisms

[Term]
id: PCO:0000004
name: quality of an ecological community
def: "A quality that inheres in a community." []
comment: Includes qualities like diversity, species richness, stability, resilience, community structure, number of trophic levels. A community quality may depend on the qualities of individual organism in the community, but cannot be measured or described for a single individual.
is_a: PATO:0002003 ! population quality
intersection_of: PATO:0002003 ! population quality
intersection_of: RO:0000052 PCO:0000002 ! characteristic of ecological community
relationship: RO:0000052 PCO:0000002 ! characteristic of ecological community

[Term]
id: PCO:0000018
name: single-species collection of organisms
def: "A material entity that has as parts two or more organisms, viruses, or viroids of the same species and no members of any other species." []
is_a: PCO:0000000 ! collection of organisms

[Term]
id: PCO:0000029
name: multi-species collection of organisms
def: "A collection of organisms that consists of two or more organisms from at least two species." []
is_a: PCO:0000000 ! collection of organisms
relationship: RO:0002351 PCO:0000001 {minCardinality="2"} ! has member population of organisms
relationship: RO:0002351 PCO:0000001 ! has member population of organisms

[Term]
id: PCO:0000031
name: organismal entity
def: "A material entity that is one or more organisms, viruses or viroids." []
is_a: BFO:0000040

